There are 18 total slices, and 10 of them have pepperoni and 10 have mushrooms.
Let there be $n$ slices that have both.  Then there are $10-n$ with only pepperoni and $10-n$ with mushrooms.  The total number of slices then is $n+(10-n)+(10-n)=18$.  Simplifying gives $20-n = 18$, so $n=\boxed{2}$:


[asy]
unitsize(0.05cm);
label("Pepperoni", (2,74));
label("Mushrooms", (80,74));
draw(Circle((30,45), 22));
draw(Circle((58, 45), 22));
label("$n$", (44, 45));
label(scale(0.8)*"$10-n$",(28,58));
label(scale(0.8)*"$10-n$",(63,58));
[/asy]

